                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_9.png" id="511-0" width=27 height=27 alt="9 polar patterns" title="Cardioid, Omni, Figure 8, and six intermediate positions" ></span>Ningbo Alctron Electronics Co., Ltd. HSGT-2B</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Multi-Pattern Tube Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The HSGT-2B is a large-diaphragm, multipattern tube mic, made in China by Alctron and sold under a variety of familiar brand names.</p><p>The specs claim the tube is a selected 6072/12AT7, but is more commonly a 12AX7 which has different characteristics and is arguably a poor fit for the mic&#8217;s schematic &#8212; leading to the common and easy mod of replacing the tube (assuming it&#8217;s socketed) with a true 6072/12AY7.</p><p>The mic ships with a power supply, 7-pin cable, spider shockmount, foam windscreen, and an aluminum road case.</p><p>Note that Alctron&#8217;s published frequency-response graphs for this mic are identical to the HST-11A, and in fact to most of their large-diaphragm tube condensers.<p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Alctron/HSGT-2B">Ningbo Alctron Electronics Co., Ltd. HSGT-2B</a> is also known as: HST-2B, GT-2B, HSGT2B.</p>
